# Shared build-context trimming. Applies to EVERY build that uses the repo root
# as its context: backend/Dockerfile (compose's `api` and the Railway `api`
# service) and deploy/hf-space/Dockerfile, which builds the React bundle and the
# backend together.
#
# Do NOT exclude `frontend` wholesale: the Space image needs frontend/ sources
# for its node build stage, and a directory excluded at the context level cannot
# be recovered by a later COPY, even for a single file inside it. Only the
# generated/vendored subtrees below are excluded.

# Virtualenvs and caches
.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/

# VCS and editor
.git/
.gitignore
.claude/
.vscode/
.idea/

# Frontend generated/vendored trees (sources themselves are kept — see above)
frontend/node_modules/
frontend/dist/
frontend/coverage/
frontend/playwright-report/
frontend/test-results/

# Secrets: compose injects .env at RUN time via `env_file`, the Space uses its
# own secret store, and Railway injects variables. It must never land in an
# image layer — anything COPYed in stays recoverable even if a later layer
# removes it.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Data: excluded wholesale, then re-included by name.
#
# docker-compose.yml bind-mounts data/ locally, but a PaaS has no bind mounts —
# an image without these two files cannot serve a request, because
# app/api/dependencies.py opens both at startup (CHUNK_STORE_PATH and
# MVP_SOURCE_CHUNKS_PATH). They are byte-identical 14 MB files.
#
# Order is load-bearing: a negation only takes effect if it FOLLOWS the pattern
# that excluded the path, and `data/**` (not `data/`) is required for a negation
# to reach a file inside an excluded subdirectory.
#
# data/raw is the copyrighted source PDFs and data/traces.db is local dev state;
# neither is re-included, so both stay out of every image.
data/**
!data/chunk_store/medical_chunks.jsonl
!data/chunks/benchmark/1.0_S1.jsonl
# The care directory backs the CTA buttons (GET /api/care-directory).
!data/care_directory.json

# Logs
*.log
